WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.940
Calcutta, eighteen fifty five.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.960
A scholar reads by lamplight,

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.910
looking for one verse.

4
00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:09.619
In the courts then, a Hindu

5
00:00:09.619 --> 00:00:11.519
widow could not make a second

6
00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:13.299
valid marriage.

7
00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:15.579
Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar set

8
00:00:15.579 --> 00:00:17.189
out to change that.

9
00:00:17.646 --> 00:00:19.706
He searched the old law books.

10
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:22.186
In the Parashara Smriti, he

11
00:00:22.186 --> 00:00:22.846
found it:

12
00:00:22.846 --> 00:00:25.826
if a husband has died, or is

13
00:00:25.826 --> 00:00:28.146
lost, a woman may take another

14
00:00:28.146 --> 00:00:29.076
husband.

15
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.980
In January eighteen fifty five,

16
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.960
he published a small pamphlet in

17
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.710
Bengali. Replies poured in.

18
00:00:37.084 --> 00:00:38.604
Instead of answering each

19
00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.464
critic, he wrote one more

20
00:00:40.464 --> 00:00:42.924
pamphlet, answering them all.

21
00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:45.494
A scholar's way of saving time.

22
00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.007
Critics said he was moved by

23
00:00:48.007 --> 00:00:50.147
pity, not the texts.

24
00:00:50.147 --> 00:00:51.307
He replied:

25
00:00:51.307 --> 00:00:53.247
"It is true that I do feel

26
00:00:53.247 --> 00:00:55.587
compassion." But he wrote only

27
00:00:55.587 --> 00:00:58.417
once sure the texts allowed it.

28
00:00:58.781 --> 00:01:00.221
He petitioned the Legislative

29
00:01:00.221 --> 00:01:02.341
Council. A counter petition

30
00:01:02.341 --> 00:01:04.621
came, with nearly four times as

31
00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:05.871
many signatures.

32
00:01:06.515 --> 00:01:09.355
Still, in eighteen fifty six,

33
00:01:09.355 --> 00:01:10.235
the law came.

34
00:01:10.235 --> 00:01:11.715
Act Fifteen:

35
00:01:11.715 --> 00:01:13.895
"to remove all legal obstacles

36
00:01:13.895 --> 00:01:15.315
to the marriage of Hindu

37
00:01:15.315 --> 00:01:16.385
widows."

38
00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:18.052
For GS1:

39
00:01:18.052 --> 00:01:19.705
a widow's remarriage became

40
00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:21.845
valid, its children legitimate.

41
00:01:21.845 --> 00:01:24.285
One catch to remember:

42
00:01:24.285 --> 00:01:26.425
she lost her rights in her late

43
00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:27.655
husband's property.

44
00:01:28.637 --> 00:01:31.757
A lamp, an old book, a patient

45
00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:35.247
argument. And a door, opened.
